# --- OpenBox desktop (minimal, no display manager, no panel) --------------
# OpenBox is the whole desktop: a lightweight X11 window manager the startx session
# execs directly (exec openbox-session in ~/.xinitrc). There is NO panel -- the Azzio
# application menu (Super key / centered popup) is the only shell surface, so no
# tint2/panel package is shipped. `xcape` turns a lone Super tap into Super+Menu
# so OpenBox's rc.xml can bind the menu launcher to the bare Super key (OpenBox
# cannot bind a lone modifier itself). `feh` (already in the manifest) paints the
# wallpaper from the OpenBox autostart. kitty is the ONE terminal (bound to W-Return
# and seeded in the menu); xterm/uxterm are deliberately NOT shipped -- the `xterm`
# package drags in both and the user does not want them. No sddm (autologin + startx).
openbox
xcape
adwaita-icon-theme
gnome-themes-extra
xcursor-themes
